# Update README after major changes

When this session adds or materially changes **user-facing capabilities**, **architecture**, **setup**, or **deployment**, update `README.md` in the **same change** — not only API docs.

## Update README when

1. New major features (V2 modules, integrations, roles, workflows)
2. New env vars or secrets users must configure
3. Docker / compose / CI / deploy path changes
4. New external data sources (e.g. govt mandi feeds, payment gateways)
5. Breaking changes to how devs run or test the project

## README sections to touch

- **What is already built** — capability table
- **Environment** / setup steps if new keys or services
- **Run locally** / Docker if commands or ports change
- Short note on data sources or third-party deps when relevant

## Skip

- Bug fixes, typos, internal refactors with no user/setup impact
- Doc-only edits outside README unless README already describes the old behavior

## Pair with

- `docs/API_CONTRACT.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` for API changes (see `update-api-docs.mdc`)
- `docs/WEEKLY_PROGRESS.md` for faculty tracker when product work ships
